<BaseLayout title="Haonan Bai | About">
  <section class="profile">
    <div><img src="/img/Picture.jpg" alt="Haonan Bai" /><p class="links"><a href="https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=K2Z8ui0AAAAJ&hl=en">Google Scholar</a><br /><a href="https://orcid.org/0009-0008-6061-107X">ORCID</a> · <a href="https://github.com/amaodemao">GitHub</a></p></div>
    <div>
      <p>
        Hi! I am a first-year Master of Applied Science student in 
          <a href="https://ece.ubc.ca/">Electrical and Computer Engineering</a>
        at the University of British Columbia. 
        Previously, I earned my Bachelor of Engineering degree in Artificial Intelligence from the 
        <a href="https://www.cse.cuhk.edu.hk/">Department of Computer Science and Engineering</a> 
        at the Chinese University of Hong Kong.
      </p>
      <p>
        My research lies at the intersection of 
        <strong>Artificial Intelligence</strong>, 
        <strong>Software Engineering</strong>, and 
        <strong>Security</strong>. 
        I am interested in building robust, safe and fair AI systems.
      </p>
      <p>
        I am currently working with Prof. Julia Rubin and Prof. Simon Oya. Previously, I had the privilege of working with 
        Prof. Michael R. Lyu and Prof. Wenxuan Wang at CUHK, as well as Prof. Xin Eric Wang at the UC Santa Barbara.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2 id="publications">Publications</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>New Job, New Gender? Measuring the Social Bias in Image Generation Models</strong>
        <div class="publication-details">
          <p>Wenxuan Wang, <b>Haonan Bai</b>, Jen-tse Huang, Yuxuan Wan, Youliang Yuan, Haoyi Qiu, Nanyun Peng, Michael R. Lyu</p>
          <p><b class="oral">[Oral presentation; 174/4,385 submissions, top 3.97%]</b> ACM Multimedia, 2024</p>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>BiasAsker: Measuring the Bias in Conversational AI System</strong>
        <div class="publication-details">
          <p>Yuxuan Wan, Wenxuan Wang, Pinjia He, Jiazhen Gu, <b>Haonan Bai</b>, Michael Lyu</p>
          <p>ESEC/FSE, 2023</p>
        </div>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

